{"id": "tea:muktika-upanisad:1-prose-knowledge-alone", "source": "src:muktika-upanisad", "location": {"ref": "1 (prose: knowledge alone)"}, "paraphrase": "Kaivalya is gained by knowledge alone — not by works, Sāṃkhya, yoga or worship.", "tags": {"level": "ultimate", "standpoint": "absolute", "naya": null, "path": ["knowledge"], "stage": "advanced"}, "types": ["karma-liberation", "dispute"], "disputes": ["dsp:yoga-or-knowledge-for-liberation"], "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": [], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "high", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "coverage": ["A2"], "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U04-minor-upanisads"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:muktika-upanisad:1-prose-the-path", "source": "src:muktika-upanisad", "location": {"ref": "1 (prose: the path)"}, "paraphrase": "One endowed with the fourfold means approaches a true guru with gifts, studies the 108, and by hearing, reflection and contemplation becomes liberated while living; when prārabdha is exhausted he gains bodiless liberation, like the space in a pot when the pot breaks.", "tags": {"level": "bridging", "standpoint": "seeker", "naya": null, "path": ["knowledge"], "stage": "intermediate"}, "types": ["practice", "karma-liberation"], "concepts": ["cpt:sadhana-catustaya", "cpt:jivanmukti", "cpt:videhamukti"], "paths": ["pth:muktika-path"], "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": [], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "high", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "coverage": ["A2"], "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U04-minor-upanisads"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:muktika-upanisad:1-prose-veda-lists", "source": "src:muktika-upanisad", "location": {"ref": "1 (prose: Veda lists)"}, "paraphrase": "The prose lists the Upaniṣads under each Veda with the peace-chant of each: Ṛgveda (vāṅ me manasi), Śukla Yajurveda (pūrṇam adaḥ), Kṛṣṇa Yajurveda (saha nāv avatu), Sāmaveda (āpyāyantu), Atharvaveda (bhadraṃ karṇebhiḥ).", "tags": {"level": "conventional", "standpoint": "analytic", "naya": null, "path": ["knowledge"], "stage": "all"}, "types": ["sound-language"], "concepts": ["cpt:muktika-canon"], "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": [], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "high", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "coverage": ["A2"], "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U04-minor-upanisads"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:muktika-upanisad:1.1-9", "source": "src:muktika-upanisad", "location": {"ref": "1.1-9"}, "paraphrase": "In Ayodhyā, Hanumān asks Rāma, seated among Sītā, his brothers and the sages, to know his nature for liberation; Rāma says he is established in Vedānta and tells him to take refuge in it: the Vedas arose as the breath of Viṣṇu, and Vedānta is established in the Veda like oil in sesame.", "tags": {"level": "conventional", "standpoint": "divine", "naya": null, "path": ["devotion"], "stage": "all"}, "types": ["teacher-transmission"], "teachers": ["tch:rama", "tch:hanuman"], "speaker": "Rāma", "addressee": "Hanumān", "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": [], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "moderate", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "coverage": ["A2"], "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U04-minor-upanisads"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:muktika-upanisad:1.12-15", "source": "src:muktika-upanisad", "location": {"ref": "1.12-15"}, "paraphrase": "The Ṛgveda has 21 branches, the Yajurveda 109, the Sāmaveda 1,000 and the Atharvaveda 50; each branch has one Upaniṣad; whoever recites even one verse of them with devotion to Rāma attains union with him.", "tags": {"level": "conventional", "standpoint": "cosmic", "naya": null, "path": ["knowledge"], "stage": "all"}, "types": ["sound-language", "teacher-transmission"], "concepts": ["cpt:muktika-canon"], "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": [], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "high", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "coverage": ["A2"], "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U04-minor-upanisads"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:muktika-upanisad:1.15-25", "source": "src:muktika-upanisad", "location": {"ref": "1.15-25"}, "paraphrase": "Some say liberation comes by chanting Rāma's name, by the tāraka at Kāśī, by Sāṃkhya-yoga, by bhakti-yoga or by inquiry into Vedānta; liberation is said to be fourfold — sālokya, sārūpya, sāmīpya, sāyujya — and these four come from worship of Rāma: even one of bad conduct reaches sālokya by his name; one who dies at Kāśī receives Rāma's tāraka from Maheśvara in the right ear and gains liberation without return (sārūpya); but kaivalya alone is the ultimate liberation.", "tags": {"level": "bridging", "standpoint": "seeker", "naya": null, "path": ["knowledge"], "stage": "intermediate"}, "types": ["karma-liberation", "death-dying"], "concepts": ["cpt:four-kinds-of-mukti", "cpt:avimukta-taraka"], "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": [], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "high", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "coverage": ["A2"], "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U04-minor-upanisads"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:muktika-upanisad:1.26-29", "source": "src:muktika-upanisad", "location": {"ref": "1.26-29"}, "paraphrase": "For liberation the Māṇḍūkya alone suffices; if knowledge does not arise, study the ten; if still not, the thirty-two; and for bodiless liberation, the hundred and eight.", "tags": {"level": "bridging", "standpoint": "seeker", "naya": null, "path": ["knowledge"], "stage": "intermediate"}, "types": ["practice", "karma-liberation"], "concepts": ["cpt:muktika-canon"], "paths": ["pth:muktika-path"], "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": [], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "high", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "coverage": ["A2"], "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U04-minor-upanisads"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:muktika-upanisad:1.30-39", "source": "src:muktika-upanisad", "location": {"ref": "1.30-39"}, "paraphrase": "The names of the 108 Upaniṣads, beginning with Īśa, Kena, Kaṭha, Praśna, Muṇḍaka, Māṇḍūkya, Taittirīya, Aitareya, Chāndogya and Bṛhadāraṇyaka and ending with the Muktikā.", "tags": {"level": "conventional", "standpoint": "analytic", "naya": null, "path": ["knowledge"], "stage": "all"}, "types": ["teacher-transmission"], "concepts": ["cpt:muktika-canon"], "notes": "The e-text reads 'mahānārāyaṇāhvayam' in 1.34 where other editions read 'mahānārāyaṇādvayam'.", "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": [], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "high", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "coverage": ["A2"], "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U04-minor-upanisads"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:muktika-upanisad:1.40-49", "source": "src:muktika-upanisad", "location": {"ref": "1.40-49"}, "paraphrase": "These 108 destroy the three bodies and give liberation; they must not be given to the unbeliever, the ungrateful, the ill-behaved or one who does not serve; they may be given to the devoted, well-tested disciple who serves — 'knowledge came to the brāhmaṇa and said: guard me, I am your treasure'.", "tags": {"level": "conventional", "standpoint": "seeker", "naya": null, "path": ["general"], "stage": "all"}, "types": ["teacher-transmission"], "concepts": ["cpt:secrecy-and-eligibility"], "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": [], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "high", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "coverage": ["A2"], "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U04-minor-upanisads"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:muktika-upanisad:2.1-13", "source": "src:muktika-upanisad", "location": {"ref": "2.1-13"}, "paraphrase": "Liberation while living is the cessation of the mind's properties; the destruction of vāsanā, knowledge of truth and the dissolution of mind must be practised together for a long time — practised singly they do not succeed.", "tags": {"level": "bridging", "standpoint": "seeker", "naya": null, "path": ["knowledge"], "stage": "intermediate"}, "types": ["consciousness-mind", "karma-liberation"], "concepts": ["cpt:vasana-ksaya-manonasa-tattvajnana", "cpt:jivanmukti"], "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": [], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "high", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "coverage": ["A2"], "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U04-minor-upanisads"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:muktika-upanisad:2.2", "source": "src:muktika-upanisad", "location": {"ref": "2.2"}, "paraphrase": "Vāsanās for the world, for scripture and for the body prevent true knowledge.", "tags": {"level": "bridging", "standpoint": "seeker", "naya": null, "path": ["knowledge"], "stage": "intermediate"}, "types": ["consciousness-mind"], "obstacles": ["obs:three-vasanas"], "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": [], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "moderate", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "coverage": ["A2"], "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U04-minor-upanisads"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:muktika-upanisad:2.26-27", "source": "src:muktika-upanisad", "location": {"ref": "2.26-27"}, "paraphrase": "The tree of mind has two seeds: the vibration of prāṇa and vāsanā; when one is stopped both cease.", "tags": {"level": "bridging", "standpoint": "seeker", "naya": null, "path": ["knowledge"], "stage": "intermediate"}, "types": ["consciousness-mind", "body-layers"], "concepts": ["cpt:vasana-ksaya-manonasa-tattvajnana"], "cross_refs": ["tea:yogakundali-upanisad:1.1"], "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": [], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "high", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "coverage": ["A2"], "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U04-minor-upanisads"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:muktika-upanisad:2.32-35", "source": "src:muktika-upanisad", "location": {"ref": "2.32-35"}, "paraphrase": "Dissolution of mind is of two kinds: with form (in the one liberated while living) and without form (in the bodiless liberated).", "tags": {"level": "ultimate", "standpoint": "absolute", "naya": null, "path": ["knowledge"], "stage": "advanced"}, "types": ["consciousness-mind", "karma-liberation"], "concepts": ["cpt:jivanmukti", "cpt:videhamukti"], "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": [], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "high", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "coverage": ["A2"], "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U04-minor-upanisads"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:muktika-upanisad:2.42-47", "source": "src:muktika-upanisad", "location": {"ref": "2.42-47"}, "paraphrase": "The means to stilling mind are knowledge of the Self, the company of the wise, abandoning vāsanās and stopping the vibration of prāṇa; trying to control the mind by force is like binding a rutting elephant with lotus fibres.", "tags": {"level": "bridging", "standpoint": "seeker", "naya": null, "path": ["knowledge"], "stage": "intermediate"}, "types": ["practice", "consciousness-mind"], "concepts": ["cpt:vasana-ksaya-manonasa-tattvajnana"], "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": [], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "high", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "coverage": ["A2"], "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U04-minor-upanisads"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:muktika-upanisad:2.53-56", "source": "src:muktika-upanisad", "location": {"ref": "2.53-56"}, "paraphrase": "Samādhi with support (samprajñāta) and without (asamprajñāta) are distinguished; the latter is the dissolution of mind.", "tags": {"level": "conventional", "standpoint": "seeker", "naya": null, "path": ["meditation"], "stage": "intermediate"}, "types": ["consciousness-mind"], "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": [], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "moderate", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "coverage": ["A2"], "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U04-minor-upanisads"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:muktika-upanisad:2.61-71", "source": "src:muktika-upanisad", "location": {"ref": "2.61-71"}, "paraphrase": "Vāsanās are pure or impure; replace impure with pure, then abandon even the pure, and even the desire for liberation. As the ladle stirs food without tasting it, the knower acts without attachment; the body is impure, the embodied Self pure.", "tags": {"level": "ultimate", "standpoint": "absolute", "naya": null, "path": ["knowledge"], "stage": "advanced"}, "types": ["consciousness-mind", "practice"], "concepts": ["cpt:vasana-ksaya-manonasa-tattvajnana"], "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": [], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "moderate", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "coverage": ["A2"], "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U04-minor-upanisads"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:muktika-upanisad:2.76", "source": "src:muktika-upanisad", "location": {"ref": "2.76"}, "paraphrase": "When the body falls the one liberated in life enters bodiless liberation, like the wind becoming still.", "tags": {"level": "ultimate", "standpoint": "absolute", "naya": null, "path": ["knowledge"], "stage": "advanced"}, "types": ["karma-liberation", "death-dying"], "concepts": ["cpt:videhamukti"], "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": [], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "high", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "coverage": ["A2"], "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U04-minor-upanisads"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
